I just got an old AlphaStation 200 4/166 from the surplus department at
my university, but I can't seem to get it to display anything on the
console (a DEC PBXGA-AA/AN PCI graphics card).

The card has a set of four DIP-switches (all in the 'closed' position)
and a mini-phone jack that are accessable from the outside, as well as a
single internal jumper (3 pins with 2 jumpered together, no indication
which is pin 1), none of whose functions are obvious. The motherboard
also has a number of jumpers at different locations, most of which are
unlabeled. The motherboard is laid out something like this:

diag-LEDs  SCSI    parallel   serial PS/2
------------------------------------------ back of case, I/O ports
| DD DD  SSSSSSSS  PPPPPPPPP   CCC   KBM |
|                            V           | V: slots for the PCI &
| BB              V          V       H H |    audio riser cards
| BB          J24 V          V       H H |
|                 V    spkr  V       H H | H: power supply headers
|J21          J22 V          V       H H |
|                 V    m m m m  m m  H H | s: internal SCSI header
|           WWWW  V    m m m m  m m   s f|
| C C C C   WdaW  V    m m m m  m m   s f| f: floppy header
| C C C C   WWWW  V    m m m m  m m   s f|
| C C C C         V    m m m m  m m J7s f| X: socketed chip
| C C C C   WWWW  V    m m m m  m m J7s f|    TMS27PC512
| C C C C   WbaW  V    m m m m  m m J6s  |
| C C C C   WWWW  V    m m m m  m m   XX | O: empty sockets, same
| C C C C         V    m m m m  m m   XX |    type as X
| C C C C         V                      |
| C C C C         V                   OO | W: motherboard chipset
| C C C C   WWWW                      OO |    DEC 21071-LL, where
| C C C C   WbaW                         |    LL={DA,BA,CA} aka
| C C C C   WWWW                      OO |    SC02RH02xDL02 where
| C C C C                             OO |    x={6,7,8}
|                 WWWW                   |
| AAAAAAAAAAAAAA  WcaW                   | A: socketed Alpha CPU
| AAAAAAAAAAAAAA  WWWW                   |
| AAAAAAAAAAAAAA                         | Y: 333MHz crystal
| AAAAAAAAAAAAAA   J30                   |
| AAAAAAAAAAAAAA  YY                     | m: memory SIMM sockets
| AAAAAAAAAAAAAA  YY                     |
| AAAAAAAAAAAAAA   J4  J29               | C: cache RAM & tags
|              J1 J2 hJ3r      J5fpnl    |
------------------------------------------ front of case
  CPU fan+vent       front panel

The jumpers I am concerned about are J1, J2, J3*, J6, J7**, J21, J22,
and J24. J4 is only a set of solder pads with no pins. J29 appears to be
a power connector for the fan. J3 has pins but no jumpers on the pins.

J1, J2, J3, and J6 are three pin headers. J1 and J2 are jumpered on pins
2 and 3. J3 is jumpered on pins 1 and 2, but I can infer from the silk
screened label that J3 controls the systems response to the reset switch
(either halt or reset, as indicated in my diagram by the notation hJ3r).
J6 is also jumpered on pins 1 and 2.

J7 is a 10-pin enclosed header, with the pins in 2 rows of 5 pins. J22
and J24 are simple 2 pin headers, jumpered shut. J21 is a 2 pin header
with the jumper in the open position (only on one pin).

So my questions are:

  1) what jumpers or switches do I have to set to get the thing
     to boot with the ROM monitor displaying on the PCI graphics
     card?

  2) what do the patterns on the diagnostic LEDs mean?

  3) what do the other jumpers do? (so long as it is something
     operationally usefull)

  4) what are the two empty sockets (labeled 'O' on my diagram)
     for? I can guess that the TI chip is some kind of EEPROM,
     which suggests that the empty sockets are for extra EEPROM
     to accomodate larger boot monitor programs, but I'm just
     guessing here and I'd like to be certain.

I've tried searching the Compaq site for usefull docs, but came up empty
handed. It's a real shame that Compaq is not making old DEC docs
available on the web.

Thanks for any help.

- Jeff Dutky


