Video card is a ZLXp-E1 (2mb);switches control resolution output; all closed
indicates 130Mhz (1280x1024) at 72Hz-be aware the console op should be set
to graphics and tga_sync should be set accordingly (sync green or not); What
monitor you use determines if console is observed.
Jumpers:
    ji=mini-console-default topin2/3
    j2=boot flashrom (pin 2/3) or boot floppy (pin 1/2)
    j3=front panel button reset (pin 1/2 defalt)
    j6=enable flashrom write (pin 1/2 default)
    j17=keyboard cont ip (default=all open)
    j21=enable scsi ext cable sense (defaultopen)
    j22=enhanced parr port (default=pin 1/2)
    j24=same as above 9(different chipset)
sockets (oo)=eproms for aternaive console (ie.,arc for NT operation)
LED codes usually indicate me/flashrom/controllers pass/fail-send an
indication of the on/off pattern and we can tell you the code
                                                Cheers,   mhr



