just got mine to boot RH6.2 and I've got the ATA2940UW on a PWS500au.

Here's the snippet from http://www.alphalinux.org/faq/milo-9.html:

"MILO does not recognise the SCSI device

The standard MILO images include as many device drivers as are known to
be stable for Alpha (as of now that includes the NCR 810, QLOGIC ISP,
Buslogic and Adaptec 2940s and 3940 cards). If your card is not
included, it may be that the driver is not stable enough on an Alpha
system yet. Again, the latest MILO images are worth trying. You can
tell which SCSI devices a MILO image has built into it by using
the "show" command."


