> but the c header files provided in the glibc rpm doesnt seem to contain lot
> of commonly
> used functions! ( for example the math.h doesnt contain the sin, cos, etc
> functions.)
Have you looked inside them? The header files only supply information
about the types of the function parameters and the return type to
the compiler. The code for 'sin/cos..' is inside libraries.
In Unix, somebody decided, that very few people use these functions,
and so there code is not in libc but in libm. So just add -lm to your
link line.

Hope that helps,
Martin.

