Mingetty works just find on the serial port, it's preferred, if you do not
want all the modem handling junk..
   HS's inittab entry is correct..

If you have serial console support and DO NOT add "console=ttyS0" to the
boot_flags (-fl) The kernel boot messages will try to display to a graphics
display and will not be directed to the serial port. Same for shutdowns,
that's why it looks silent.   If there is NO graphics card present
(Physically Removed), the kernel will automatically redirect to the serial
port, if its built into the kernel.

So:
 Graphics + Serial  console support + NO "console=ttyS0"  =
                   ttyS0 only displays the login prompt after bootup
completes

Graphics  + Serial console support+ "console=ttyS0"  =
                   ttyS0 displays the bootup kernel messages and init
messages..

 No graphics card installed  + serial console support + NO "console=ttyS0" =
                    Kernel redirects to serial console on ttyS0 (if present)
else panics.

JJ


