After you get into fdisk and type "b" to get the "bsd disklabel" mode, there
is a command which will print out the entire label, including the drive
characteristics (cyl/head/sectors) type a "m" and look at the options, I
think it's  "s"  or a letter around the high end..

Sounds like you have a Cylinder wrap,  (writing past the last cylinder and
wrapping to the start of the disk)

If you can get a jumpstart CD (download & burn) It makes the setup a lot
easier..
But if not, Star your First partition on cyl 2,  and if its a old dist (5.2)
stop at lastcyl-1)

