Haven't really kept up on this lately but here's my experience on a 500
pc164 board: scsi cont supported; most ncr 810s, any qlogic (esp 1020, but
1040 as well) the Intraservers are great for fast (even those not supported
by VMS/tru64)-only problem found was mixing the slow 810 (cd/tape) with the
fast Intraservers-lots of timeouts (however not a problem with VMS and
tru64). Using Elsa Gloria, no ide, mostly dec 21143 nics (Intraserver will
save a slot, 21143 is scsi cont mounted);tlz tapes fine panasonic/mashi..
,toshiba (scsi for all)cd's rz type hds fine, quantums fine, ibms fine Have
loaded and booted both Suse 6.2 and RH6.1 with no problem. I copied the srm
file according to the update instructions on the firmware page using an
existing VMS system with absolutely no problems; Although I usually run VMS,
I still boot both the RH and Suse drives occassionally to check some of the
newer software avalible. I haven't really used ARC for a few years (and had
nothing but trouble with it then) but I assume you can just type update at
the console and it will look first a dva0 for the srm file. Good luck

mhr




