Hello Mike!

Jensen type machines like the (Highscreen?) AXP 150 have only 2 banks of
4 sockets each. (BTW the sockets are interleaved, like even vs. odd.) So
the four 4MB simms constitute one bank instead of two. The jensen will
interleave(?) its to banks to widen the memory bus from 64 to 128bit(?).
So it might be that mixing diffent sized simms will result in odd
results like showing only 4MB of each 16 Mb but I am wildly speculating
here. Anyway, I would be surprised if the widening of the memory bus
could be achieved with unequal simms (at least if it is done by
interleaving the banks). 

Good luck
	Sebastian Moeller 

