You have this problem because SRM and Alphabios store the year in different
formats in cmos.   It wasn't bad till they also removed the "date" command
from SRM console so you could not reset the time when it gets corrupted..
like when you run the ECU or RCU from SRM which invokes alphabios.

Jumpstart 1.1 checks/fixes the date as part of it setup.

to see if the date command is in your firmware, just type "date" at the
"srm" prompt  >>>

JJ

