I've seen this before. Is there anything attached to the serial ports? 
If so remove it! Even then you may have to power the system off for a 
while before the drive is detected again. Is this a Samsung or 
Deskstation produced board? IIRC the Deskstation made boards had some
problems with the ethernet and floppy controllers. The ethernet is 
fixable, but I haven't yet found a solution to the floppy vanishing.

Did you put "ldmilo" on the boot disk? In addition to milo, Ruffians 
need ldmilo because they have ARCS BIOS (note the "S"). 

As for which distro: try a couple of them. I personally recommend Debian 
GNU/Linux. 

