There are a few other things I can add here:

1) If boot without gfx card doesn't work, try hooking up a monitor,
keyboard, and mouse too.
2) Be sure your term is set for 9600-8-n-1.  Not guaranteed to be right,
but almost.
3) Try switching serial ports
4) Wait 3-4 minutes before declaring the thing non-functional.  With some
old machines, it can take that long.
5) On serial port, tap enter key a few times.
6) If you get through any of these ways, and if you get a srm prompt, you
might want to use the following commands:
  >>> set console serial
  >>> set quick_start on

