which dist do you have?
The current kernels are built with serial console enabled

just add "console=ttyS0"  to the -fl string you boot with, or if you use
aboot.conf, add "console=ttyS0" to the entries.
(example boot  dka0 -fi 2/boot/vmlinuz -fl "root=/dev/sda2 console=ttyS0")
You do not need to specify the ttyS0 parameters, the defaults are correct.
Now... a little additional.

You have to add a "getty" to  /etc/inittab so you can get a prompt.  Copy
the tty6 entry, make it 7: and the device is /dev/ttyS0

Edit "/etc/securetty"  and add ttyS0, so you can login as root on ttyS0..

This works for me

JJ



