To follow up on this, the power supply arrived and works well with the
PC64.  Curiously, my board is labelled "PC64", but the layout does not
quite match the connector diagrams in the PC64 User Guide available
online.  Some checking around on the board with a continuity tester
confirmed the pinouts before I connected the PS.

Word of warning, this power supply does not have a power switch and
depends on the power signal from the motherboard, which the Cabriolet does
not provide.  The easy workaround is to connect an SPST switch to the
green/black leads from the PS and use that instead.  Works like a charm.

Thanks again for the info.  I have been trying to find this PS for a
while.

