MLS <mseganti@optonline.net> schrieb in im Newsbeitrag:
39EBC969.869AC13F@optonline.net...
> Hi all,
> I'm installing RH6.2 on an AS200 w/ 1 GB scsi internal.  I setup the
> partitions as 2 cylinders unused, 16Mb for /boot, 64 Mb Swap and 900+
> for /.  All goes well, until the install phase.  At this point, it tells
> me I need 25Mb for the / mount point.  It should have 900+ at this
> point.
>
> The only thing I can think of is that the install is using the CD as
> the root, since I booted via the SRM using:
>
> >>> boot dka400 -file kernels/generic.gz -flags "root=/dev/scd0"
>
> note: /dev/scd0 - is an external scsi CD drive.  The system won't boot
> without that flag set to the CD.
>
> Any suggestions would be appreciated.
>
> Thanks,
> Mike...

Your boot-command is correct, but you will go into the grafic-mode while
installing
which will not work on the as200 (my be you have another graficboard - i
have a dec-tga with 8 planes)
so you can add the option "text" as below.

>>> boot dka400 -file kernels/generic.gz -flags "text root=/dev/scd0"

But don't wast additional time, rh 6.2 doesn't work on the as200

Try debian2.2 (potato) this installs fine on the as200
You enter boot dka400 from the srm, which will lead you to aboot

then the "l" command will show the available kernels on the CD.
enter "0" for booting with console=graphics , 1 for console is COM1 etc.

The rest goes without any complications and is wonderfull guided...

good luck

Erich





