Ah, so much confusion.

If you want to boot a floppy disk, you need to get the files

ftp://phyppro1.phy.bnl.gov/pub/mirror/redhat-main/redhat/redhat-6.2/alpha/images/generic.img


ftp://phyppro1.phy.bnl.gov/pub/mirror/redhat-main/redhat/redhat-6.2/alpha/images/ramdisk.img

generic.img makes the bootable floppy
ramdisk.img makes the root floppy.
Insert bootable floppy, use
    b dva -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1"
or
    b dva -fl 0
    (This is a pre-configured thing for aboot)



