> Raj.

What kind?  I used pmfirewall to set up ipchains.  pmfirewall is a very well
written shell script that asks you questions, then generates ipchains rules
into a script to be run at boot.

I also got and recompiled portsentry and logcheck, both from
www.psionic.com.  portsentry watches incoming connections, and logcheck will
parse your /var/log/messages on a regular basis (providing you give it a
cron entry, of course) and email you what has happened since the last run.

Pretty much if you can get the source code for it, it should compile.




