I read french a little, but not perfect.  I think I understand everything
nico and bertrand wrote.

I think that your computer had Tru64 installed, and now you want to use
Linux instead.  But you never made linux work yet.  If this is right, you
don't want to use root=/dev/sda of any kind, because linux was never in
the hard drive.  Instead, you need to use floppies or CD.
Here's something to try:
Download through FTP the boot disk, and the root disk together.  The boot
disk is sometimes also named the rescue disk.
Put in the rescue disk, and use this line:
b dva  -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/fd0  load_ramdisk=1"
You will see a prompt "Please insert floppy disk that contains root
filesystem"

