Which system???  . some used ide CDROM's.... and some use IDE w/scsi
emulation in srm console.

To boot a SCSI CD

>>>boot dka400  -fi kernels/generic.gz  -fl "root=/dev/scd0  expert text"
****dka400 = assumes scsi cd is scsi-id 4, do a "show dev" at the console to
see what it is..

IDE CROM's can be reported as either a dk or dq device, depending on
firmware emulation..

Assuming dq   (IDE CDROM)

>>>boot  dqa0 -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/hda bootdevice=hda
expert text"

assuming a dk   (IDE CDROM with SCSI emu in SRm console,  the first actual
scsi ctrlr would be reported as dkb* )

>>>boot dka0 -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/hda bootdevice=hda expert
text"

JJ


