Hallo David!

 DW> I am running RedHat 6.2 on a DEC 166 MHz Multia (UDB).  The 
 DW> box has connectors for sound in and out, but I am unable to get 
 DW> sound out of the box.  I have tried the CD players in Gnome and
KDE, but 
 DW> it seems to me that I need to do something with the sndconfig.

Conventionally, a CD player requires an audio cable between the CD's
audio out and the Sound cards CD-in connector. This is no different on
alpha. You could use an external cable to connect the CD ROM's
headphone connector with the Multia's external line-in connetcor, and
then use a mixer to enable line-in sound.

Or you can use a digital audio grabber to rip wav-Files from the CD,
and then use a wave-Player to play the sound. There are also some
grabbers that can "play" the CD on the fly this way.

 DW> Has anyone out there successfully gotten the sound to work 
 DW> on a Multia?  If so, I would appreciate some guidance.

I never tried playing CD's, but playing Wave-Files worked for me. You
need to configure a "Microsoft Sound System" device in the kernel.

