when I boot RHLinux 6.2 from SCSI disk 1 at the SRM prompt, my command is:

boot dka0 -file 3/boot/vmlinuz-2.2.14-6.0 -flags "root=/dev/sda3"

You can set "boot_file" environment variable to: 3/boot/vmlinuz-2.2.14-6.0;
"boot_osflags" to: root=/dev/sda3; and "boot_dev" to dka0 and then all you
need to do is type >>>boot and away you go.

The boot line above assumes that I have my / directory in partition 3.  If
you created a /boot partition then the number preceding the image name would
be the partition number of the /boot partition.

Hope you get it figured out.

javanic


