> I have a Jensen with a DEC4220 NIC.
> Is there a special way to switch from coax to TP?
>
I don't have any documentation showing 'DEC4220' as a valid part number
or model name.  The DEC Etherworks EISA ethernet controller manual (which
is for the card that came in our Jensen) shows a shunt on the card (it
looks like a connected set of jumpers) on a set with three rows of pins.

If the shunt s connecting the top and middle row of pins (1 - 2) then the
thinwire should be selected.  If it is connecting middle to bottom row
(2 - 3) then the 10Base-T should be selected.

Hope that helps...

Rich Jordan
rjordan@mcs.net




