I tried very hard to make a NVIDIA TNT card work on my alpha.
I failed.

Main reason: The flash rom on gfx cards contain code.
This is x86 code.

For Alpha to use this code, it has to emulate an x86
processor.

And your alpha does just that :-)

However, the emulator for your alpha (which if I recall 
correctly) is included in MILO, only does 8086 emulation.
It cannot handle the 16 and 32 bit opcodes.

Now, in order to make a gfx card with a ROM containing
these opcodes (as nVidia's cards do) work on your alpha
you could use a third party emulator, which I think
was called em86.

This emulator DOES feature full emulation.
However, I did not succeed in integrating this
improved emulator into MILO.

As it is now, my alpha freezes up during
boot (AlphaBIOS) or without video (SRM) with
an nvidia card in it.

I suspect that GeForces use the same illegal opcodes
as the tnt's do.

My efforts were done more than a year ago now.
Maybe MILO is now in a better shape. Talk to MILO experts
I would say...
See if em86 is still alive.

     Bram


