> upgrade seems to be insuficient. Is my machine broken? Compaq tech
> support in Spain doesn't help too much... :-(

We had this problem on a number of UP2000 machines recently. The answer to 
what it is apparently depends upon the vector number that is associated 
with the error messages. If it's 0x630 (from memory) then that (in our 
case) means that the CPUs themselves are unhappy - something to do with 
onboard cache problems.

I would recommend replacing RAM first, then trying new CPUs. Failing that, 
it might be a motherboard problem.

Brian

