Hi,

on the XFree86 Homepage, the NVIDIA is listed as available driver
in 4.0.1, so in theory, you should be able to run XWindows on
the Geforce.
The only issue would be that until the X server's init, you won't
probably get any output from the card.

You could try to run the Geforce in parallel with another supported
card (old ISA-VGA for example) which you use to boot the system.
The Xserver would be configured to use the Geforce as soon as the
system is up.
If you have two monitors (or one with switchable inputs) this could
make a cool dualhead system with one graphic display and one text-
mode console.

Another approach would be to set up the system using a supported
card and when everything is complete, power down, exchange cards
and power up. Of course, there won't be any output until the
Xserver comes up which makes the boot process difficult to observe.

Note: I didn't try anything of the above, I'm using a Matrox
Millennium which works fine with linux/Alpha. Let me know what
you've done.

