Is /boot/System.map symlinked to the proper System.map-whatever file?
init needs a file named /boot/System.map or a symlink to a real file.
I use this script once I compile a new kernel:

/boot/relink
-----

#!/bin/sh

if [ $# -ne 2 ]; then
        echo "Usage: relink <kernel> <system map>"
fi

rm System.map vmlinuz
ln -s $1 vmlinuz
ln -s $2 System.map

exit 0

-----

I just have to put the kernel and System.map file somewhere (usually in
/boot) and run this 'relink' script.  That way I never forget to set
the symlinks.  The bootloader knows to look for /boot/vmlinuz so I never
have to change its setup.  Works for me.

Regards,

Tony Hammitt



